{"parentUuid":"7e6ebaaf-7bc5-495a-9861-f0dba6ec51fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgizvVeJPot5EaX92Jk6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKVUyDVWU5BpntgFom7tyf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/badges.md\"\ns=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"\"\"- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"\n## Who owns what\n\nThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n\n| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n\nThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\nthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\nuntil it moves to Praxis.\n\"\"\")\nb=\"- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\\n\"\nassert s.count(b)==1\ns=s.replace(b,\"- Where the use layer lives.\\n\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: sealing in Descartes, design in Praxis, use elsewhere\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1; entire brain remember \"Badges are split by authority: sealing (compute and seal the result, digests, embedded reference, signing) lives in Descartes; design (visual form, metadata schema, rules) lives in Praxis; use (which badges, hosting, status window) lives in a third place not yet named (Sloane 2026-11-04).\" --path architecture.badges.ownership --agent none --json 2>&1 | grep -m1 '\"id\"'","description":"Record the three-way ownership in the badge standard and in Brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":222949,"output_tokens":1402,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":369},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1402,"cache_read_input_tokens":222949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QKVUyDVWU5BpntgFom7tyf":{"command":"cd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/badges.md\"\ns=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"\"\"- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"\n## Who owns what\n\nThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n\n| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n\nThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\nthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\nuntil it moves to Praxis.\n\"\"\")\nb=\"- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\\n\"\nassert s.count(b)==1\ns=s.replace(b,\"- Where the use layer lives.\\n\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: sealing in Descartes, design in Praxis, use elsewhere\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1; entire brain remember \"Badges are split by authority: sealing (compute and seal the result, digests, embedded reference, signing) lives in Descartes; design (visual form, metadata schema, rules) lives in Praxis; use (which badges, hosting, status window) lives in a third place not yet named (Sloane 2026-11-04).\" --path architecture.badges.ownership --agent none --json 2>&1 | grep -m1 '\"id\"'","description":"Record the three-way ownership in the badge standard and in Brain"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01QKVUyDVWU5BpntgFom7tyf":{"cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"43a9466a-ade4-4b08-a9fa-72c358809245","apiBlockIndex":1,"re