sign draft","+until it moves to Praxis."," "," ## Open"," "," - The status window (the prototype used one day)."," - Hosting for status badges and claim pages."," - Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).","-- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.","+- Where the use layer lives."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"43a9466a-ade4-4b08-a9fa-72c358809245","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","root":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","branch":"ec-ai-corpus","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":14},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8696acc5-cc4c-41fc-84ce-b2aa83015fb1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"d7ee7a8d-35dd-4fb1-a04b-9f7da44a5769","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md","snippet":"39\t## Both kinds\n40\t\n41\t- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n42\t  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n43\t- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n44\t  and the check output.\n45\t- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n46\t  rests on and what rests on it.\n47\t\n48\t## Who owns what\n49\t\n50\tThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n51\t\n52\t| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n53\t|---|---|---|\n54\t| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n55\t| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n56\t| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n57\t\n58\tThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\n59\tthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\n60\tuntil it moves to Praxis.\n61\t\n62\t## Open\n63\t\n64\t- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n65\t- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n66\t- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n67\t- Where the use layer lives.","rereadEntry":{"timestamp":1793846042782,"contentHash":"356km4v9r1hwj","contentLength":3186}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"58507704-19b8-4582-b4f1-e4865ee49575","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:34:07.423Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n39\t## Both kinds\n40\t\n41\t- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n42\t  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n43\t- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n44\t  and the check output.\n45\t- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n46\t  rests on and what rests on it.\n47\t\n48\t## Who owns what\n49\t\n50\tThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n51\t\n52\t| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n53\t|---|---|---|\n54\t| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n55\t| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n56\t| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n57\t\n58\tThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\n59\tthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\n60\tuntil it moves to Praxis.\n61\t\n62\t## Open\n63\t\n64\t- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n65\t- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n66\t- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n67\t- Where the use layer lives.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","hash":"4eebce1221a21b48b64cbbcae5cb5471d17678f0302c31c7984daca6e37a50f7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKVUyDVWU5BpntgFom7tyf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/badges.md\"\ns=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"\"\"- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"\n## Who owns what\n\nThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n\n| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n\nThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\nthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\nuntil it moves to Praxis.\n\"\"\")\nb=\"- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\\n\"\nassert s.count(b)==1\ns=s.replace(b,\"- Where the use layer lives.\\n\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: sealing in Descartes, design in Praxis, use elsewhere\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg10.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1; entire brain remember \"Badges are split by authority: sealing (compute and seal the result, digests, embedded reference, signing) lives in Descartes; design (visual form, metadata schema, rules) lives in Praxis; use (which badges, hosting, status window) lives in a third place not yet named (Sloane 2026-11-04).\" --path architecture.badges.ownership --agent none --json 2>&1 | grep -m1 '\"id\"'","description":"Record the three-way ownership in the badge standard and in Brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","hash":"5198001a70f881822cc21e36135476fd18660ad0db0c9bea4c31ae5810052882","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n39\t## Both kinds\n40\t\n41\t- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n42\t  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n43\t- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n44\t  and the check output.\n45\t- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n46\t  rests on and what rests on it.\n47\t\n48\t## Who owns what\n49\t\n50\tThree owners, split by authority (Sloane, 2026-11-04):\n51\t\n52\t| Layer | Lives in | Owns |\n53\t|---|---|---|\n54\t| Sealing | Descartes | Computing the result and sealing it into the badge: the check, the digests, the embedded reference, signing. A Rust command beside `check`. |\n55\t| Design | Praxis | What a badge looks like and what it must carry: the visual form, the metadata schema, the rules on this page, shared by every Praxis producer. |\n56\t| Use | still to be named (not this repository by default) | What to do with badges: which to issue, where they're embedded and hosted, how long a status lasts. |\n57\t\n58\tThe prototype (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a\n59\tthrowaway script and belongs to none of them. This page is the design draft\n60\tuntil it moves to Praxis.\n61\t\n62\t## Open\n63\t\n64\t- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n65\t- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n66\t- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n67\t- Where the use layer lives."}]}}
