{"parentUuid":"e37a2933-34b3-4efe-98d0-b86658dac3a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8fe5717d-77b7-4c65-b625-cd66efe91f27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zss3eQwGtgZf3Dh2ahrii","type":"tool_result","content":"## Portal purpose, proposed meta-license and activity signals — 2026-11-04\n\nMaintainer feedback `msg_01M6MFC6DDG9GD21WJC0D46E7Z` asks for explicit purpose,\nbenefits, meta-license context and disclosure of intent/activity aggregation that\nreturns useful signals to activists. Interpret “metal license” as the existing\nmeta-license proposal, not a newly selected license. Praxis `docs/portal-intent.md`\nnow holds draft public copy; it is linked by the root README and contribution review.\nExplain shared evidence, challenge/correction, coordinated research and protected\ngroup access; account creation and client/owner authority remain distinct.\n\nDescribe reciprocity, attribution/provenance, reuse and returning improvements as\nproposed intent. Software/data/research terms, exceptions and allocation rules remain\nunsettled; preserve upstream rights and do not invent an enacted license, universal\ntraining permission or automatic terms acceptance from reading/signing a response.\n\nReuse the existing disclosed search/activity contribution plan and protected\nanonymization components. Specify actual events, purposes, collection surfaces,\nretention, participant controls and recipients before collection. Distinguish\nstated intent from searches/clicks/votes; do not infer an individual's political\nplans from passive activity. Keep raw/pseudonymous events restricted and separate\nfrom public contribution attribution and confidential source identity.\n\nThe shared output is a separately reviewed aggregate release: coarse topics and\nperiods, contributor bounds, defined denominator/coverage, no raw text, precise\nlocation/time or stable identifiers. Test sparse and sensitive cohorts, repeated\nreleases, differencing and external linkage; minimum group size alone proves no\nanonymity. Withhold/coarsen outputs that cannot meet the claim. No individual activist\nranking or disclosure of organizing networks. State current collection accurately:\nthis amendment activates no community telemetry or aggregate publication. Never\nsay raw tracking is anonymous merely because release processing later removes names.\n\n### Browser disclosure, optional Tauri client and bot boundaries\n\nFollow-up `msg_01M6MG8ZVE6CKM2NKQY0GJK8TN` adds EU/German privacy, an optional\napp invitation, bot resistance and Descartes evidence. “Tori” is interpreted as\nthe existing Tauri direction (N1 and the October ecosystem spike). Browser reading\nremains useful without an account, app or optional activity sharing. No client\nrelease was established by this scoped inspection: do not advertise a download\nyet. Native permissions are feature-specific; preview what leaves the device and\nits destination, with pause/revoke/cache deletion and no blanket install consent.\n\nThe portable reader source has no application analytics collector/Set-Cookie\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7e1705c1-4baa-422c-8d56-bf8811f5233a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T03:42:27.596Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Portal purpose, proposed meta-license and activity signals — 2026-11-04\n\nMaintainer feedback `msg_01M6MFC6DDG9GD21WJC0D46E7Z` asks for explicit purpose,\nbenefits, meta-license context and disclosure of intent/activity aggregation that\nreturns useful signals to activists. Interpret “metal license” as the existing\nmeta-license proposal, not a newly selected license. Praxis `docs/portal-intent.md`\nnow holds draft public copy; it is linked by the root README and contribution review.\nExplain shared evidence, challenge/correction, coordinated research and protected\ngroup access; account creation and client/owner authority remain distinct.\n\nDescribe reciprocity, attribution/provenance, reuse and returning improvements as\nproposed intent. Software/data/research terms, exceptions and allocation rules remain\nunsettled; preserve upstream rights and do not invent an enacted license, universal\ntraining permission or automatic terms acceptance from reading/signing a response.\n\nReuse the existing disclosed search/activity contribution plan and protected\nanonymization components. Specify actual events, purposes, collection surfaces,\nretention, participant controls and recipients before collection. Distinguish\nstated intent from searches/clicks/votes; do not infer an individual's political\nplans from passive activity. Keep raw/pseudonymous events restricted and separate\nfrom public contribution attribution and confidential source identity.\n\nThe shared output is a separately reviewed aggregate release: coarse topics and\nperiods, contributor bounds, defined denominator/coverage, no raw text, precise\nlocation/time or stable identifiers. Test sparse and sensitive cohorts, repeated\nreleases, differencing and external linkage; minimum group size alone proves no\nanonymity. Withhold/coarsen outputs that cannot meet the claim. No individual activist\nranking or disclosure of organizing networks. State current collection accurately:\nthis amendment activates no community telemetry or aggregate publication. Never\nsay raw tracking is anonymous merely because release processing later removes names.\n\n### Browser disclosure, optional Tauri client and bot boundaries\n\nFollow-up `msg_01M6MG8ZVE6CKM2NKQY0GJK8TN` adds EU/German privacy, an optional\napp invitation, bot resistance and Descartes evidence. “Tori” is interpreted as\nthe existing Tauri direction (N1 and the October ecosystem spike). Browser reading\nremains useful without an account, app or optional activity sharing. No client\nrelease was established by this scoped inspection: do not advertise a download\nyet. Native permissions are feature-specific; preview what leaves the device and\nits destination, with pause/revoke/cache deletion and no blanket install consent.\n\nThe portable reader source has no application analytics collector/Set-Cookie","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1ca4e9a9-1b2d-478a-9a18-ae75a91df7fa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","root":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","branch":"ec-ai-corpus","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":14},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e37a2933-34b3-4efe-98d0-b86658dac3a2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
