{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"635bb659-c1fe-4cf0-a660-c0b5574c77a5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T03:42:57.057Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"abdbf879f1c8baf4d3d130a8ccbe0672e594508c87565d961c1f493173127f1f","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"7fc10ae5-3bd6-409a-8d0c-745e43eb916b","keep":171,"tail":["1011f9878d5cd5bcb1b4fab6e861c8f0d8129ae84025893694b7887b5b8f138d","72e794574b2d33ca378e686a2b0c9daa31d0145a87d5de09371c50a0f1273d92"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",172,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"6667dbb49324ffdf903dbe404fbdaf26f3cf62c554f0e2ff6f8014a1750d1c81"}
{"parentUuid":"17455ff4-3fc9-491f-a9cf-7580e5835efa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01PpfYPMjmKB1tF1cy5bUELn","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7a5ee43a-c67b-46a1-832e-34970b5acbd9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T03:43:04.584Z","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"7a5ee43a-c67b-46a1-832e-34970b5acbd9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj6CG4FguCJPBqhn6qDh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That reframes the use layer as licensing plus offline use. I've added it to trail #29, and `docs/badges.md` now points there (pushed as `9f00cac`).\n\n**One hard limit worth stating:** once data is on someone's device, nothing technical stops them misusing it. Copy protection doesn't hold up, and it would fail activists before it slowed a company down. So the handshake can't be a lock.\n\n**What a handshake can do:**\n- **Bind the terms to the data.** The licence and permitted purpose travel inside each citation's embedded data, so they can't be separated from it.\n- **Make use attributable.** A licence would be a signed grant: who, what, for which purpose, until when. A commercial user has to be able to show one, so unlicensed commercial use becomes provable rather than prevented.\n- **Expire like a status badge.** The data and its citations stay durable, while the grant is dated, scoped and lapses. Revoking a licence means letting it expire, not reaching into anyone's device.\n- **Leave real enforcement to the contract and the law.** The handshake supplies the evidence for that.\n\n**The activist-phone case fits what we already have:**\n- **Small and self-checking.** A citation badge is about 2.7 KB and carries its own reference, so it can be verified with no network, just by recomputing hashes.\n- **Readable by a local model.** It can read the embedded data directly, with no service in between.\n- **The verifier could plausibly go on the phone.** Descartes is small Rust, so a mobile build seems feasible. I haven't tested it.\n\nThis is the use side of the central plan's proposed meta-license. The plan says not to invent an enacted licence or automatic acceptance of terms, so I've recorded these as design notes, not decisions.\n\nThree new questions are on the trail:\n- **The grant:** what form the signed grant takes, which waits on the signing-key question.\n- **The commercial line:** where it's drawn, which is a licence-terms decision, not an engineering one.\n- **The phone package:** what goes in it and how big it can be."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":728,"cache_read_input_tokens":236031,"output_tokens":668,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":728,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":236031,"cache_creation_input_tokens":728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":728},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a6ea75a3-e9a8-4e55-a4ca-2f3b076ca62b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgj6CFsM4eectUwpXPdXm","requestRef":"635bb659-c1fe-4cf0-a660-c0b5574c77a5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"044679b9-ed31-49b8-bcbe-9322afc21d32","timestamp":"2026-11-05T03:43:04.583Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
