rm economics\" (~line 3077), are where this lands.\n- Constraints the plan already records:\n  - A citation or graph path alone is not a payable entitlement.\n  - The compensation formula must be reconciled with at-cost promises, signed terms and counsel/ADV before any collection or payout. Ethical Capital is a registered adviser.\n  - The draft platform terms (section 4) restrict disclosure of fees and rate cards, which conflicts with open financials.\n  - Research reservations, platform price and upstream allocation stay separate. No automatic percentage or payout.\n\nDesign notes (Claude; proposals):\n- Price per credit = at-cost sustainability + firm margin + network margin. Each term is computed from records (metered cost, a published margin rate) and shown in a shadow calculation before any collection, which the plan already asks for.\n- Network margin allocation is computed from the contribution ledger (trail #30 questions 1–2), never assigned by hand. Graph credit (because-ness of a contributed support or fork) is one candidate input, but per the plan a graph path alone doesn't create an entitlement.\n- \"Degree of extraction\" needs a measurable definition: what is consumed (credits, bytes, queries) against what is returned (contributions). The maker-taker ratio is a natural candidate.\n- Agents in the workspace need the same handshake as people: an identity, a grant, and their contributions recorded to an owner.\n\nMore questions:\n6. The definition and measure of the degree of extraction.\n7. The firm and network margin rates, and who sets them (counsel/ADV first).\n8. Agent identity and grants inside the workspace.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc=$?; entire trail show 30 --project et/ec1c 2>&1 | grep -c \"network margin\"; entire brain remember \"Praxis API pricing direction: price per credit = at-cost sustainability of the firm + firm margin + network margin; the network margin compensates contributors who manufacture insight. The workspace is the safe collaborative space (agents welcome); extraction outside it is charged by degree. Subject to counsel/ADV and the central plan (Sloane 2026-11-04, Entire trail #30).\" --path project.commons.pricing --agent none --json 2>&1 | grep -m1 '\"id\"'","description":"Add the boundary and two-margin pricing to trail #30 and Brain"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4719c7fa-07c5-4e54-8fbf-a32d5e2542d8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgj85PKN4eSxDzeW1zZfN","requestRef":"8054253f-b1c8-4ab1-92f0-425583c6f0bd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0dbd51af-b567-400e-bf33-956731b9d303","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:07:53.405Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
