 and separate client portal\nCurrent person, relationship, resource and action.\nEvidence and argument\nResearch, models, company records and Rawls\nExact version, relevant target, provenance and qualifications.\nReview and release\nReports, aggregates, presentations and branches\nPermitted output, accountable decision and stable edition.\nMeasurement\nParsing, queries, rendering and model calls\nTime, resources, tokens, retries and coverage of the measurement.\nPrefer maintained parsers, cryptographic libraries and storage engines over homemade replacements. Compare the full dependency and maintenance cost, then test their boundaries.\nBring the software repository into the capability inventory once identified. Keep its code authority there; the lake holds governed metadata and permitted artifacts. DuckLake does not replace access control.\nThe maintainer does not recall the repository or visualization locator. Keep discovery bounded and inspect existing catalogs before creating a replacement.\n2\nHow do ideas become connected, reusable work?\nA contribution needs an inspectable path from source to claim, relevant target and intended use. New questions enter bounded triage; relevant disagreement re\n....\nOne requirements view, reusable parts and protected inputs · Archify\nSkip to content\nOne requirements view, reusable parts and protected inputs\nSystem\nLight\nDark\nEditorial\nClean\nEditorial\nProduct\nSwiss\nExport\nLong image\nPNG\nSharpest\nWebP\nSmallest\nJPG\nOpens anywhere\nPrint / PDF\nA\nAnswer\nCompose Praxis from existing capabilities, with one requirement and priority view. Publish selected works and reviewed aggregates; keep their underlying records protected.\nReuse tools before writing code; preserve clear ownership and measured costs.\nLink contributions, models, company evidence and affected-party evaluations through inspectable arguments.\nShare identity while granting community, client and automation access explicitly.\nPreserve delivered edi