{"parentUuid":"b7764e41-1150-4018-a386-7e708c2790cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8fc9E99FHQoRE9dAH6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The research found that no one has published the share of vendor sustainability-data revenue that comes from nonprofit sources. I'm adding that to trail #30 as unpinned leads and noting your point on comments versus dissent in the comments standard.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9157,"cache_read_input_tokens":260478,"output_tokens":1827,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":313},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1827,"cache_read_input_tokens":260478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d97f2817-f0e1-46d8-9f32-f50669721e75","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgj8fboPxmMAdhvLTVnbe","requestRef":"9f79fad2-32e1-4c95-b0d9-50aa0cc818ab","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec684082-1969-4422-8ea8-c779eccbe9b5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:15:25.955Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"ec684082-1969-4422-8ea8-c779eccbe9b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8fc9E99FHQoRE9dAH6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RXwYYNpxWEhP3EddmRNiHd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat >> $S/trail-commons.md <<'EOF'\n\nResearch on the extraction benchmark (LLM agent, 2026-11-04; leads, NOT pinned; no figure may enter a price until its source is pinned):\n- Market (vendors' \"ESG data\" term): Opimas is the only running series. $617M in 2019 (primary summary); over $1B in 2021; $1.9B in 2023 (Reuters citing Opimas); about $2.2B forecast for 2025 (Responsible Investor citing Opimas, Oct 2025; paywalled). The method is proprietary. MSCI's Sustainability and Climate segment had $384.8M in annual recurring revenue at 30 Sep 2026 (MSCI Q3 release).\n- Share from nonprofit sources: NOT PUBLISHED anywhere the agent could reach. MSCI and RepRisk name NGO, academic and government inputs without weights. CDP itself sells data (cdp.net/en/data-licenses) and, in June 2026, announced a split with Permira investing in a for-profit arm. That case bears directly on the commons argument.\n- Precedents: Wikimedia Enterprise $8.30M revenue in FY2024-25 (audited); CDP £60.46M income in FY2024-25, with £10.62M of charitable trading that includes data sales (not broken out); OpenCorporates offers free share-alike or paid plans (no revenue found).\n- Training-data prices: Reddit, $203.0M in aggregate data-licensing contracts over 2–3 years (S-1, primary); News Corp and OpenAI, over $250M over five years (WSJ, from sources).\n- To compute the nonprofit share properly: vendor revenue by product line (Opimas, paywalled); which inputs feed which product (methodology documents); input weights (possibly surfaced by the EU ESG ratings regulation's transparency rules); upstream licence fees actually paid; and an allocation rule between raw inputs and vendor analysis. Each is a research task in its own right.\n\nTouchpoint map (draft, Sloane's tray: touchpoints.html): every way people touch the commons (read, cite, dissent, bring evidence, answer questions, take a task, contribute code, bring an agent, license data, train a model, report a vulnerability), with what exists, the workflow, the review, the representations asked, and open questions OQ-D1..OQ-L3 attached to each touchpoint. Principle (Sloane): verification, not comments. The verification chain (colophon) makes dissent clean: dissent names a claim at a version.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc=$?; python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/comments-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## Channels\\n\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## Dissent beats comments\n\nA free-text comment can't be checked, so it adds noise as easily as signal\n(Sloane, 2026-11-04). The verification chain at the end of every rendering\n(its colophon) gives each claim a version, a source and a result. The\nstrongest response therefore names what it disputes: a claim, at a commit,\nwith a reason and, where possible, a pinned counter-source. It enters as a\nfork of the argument graph, beside ours, not as an overwrite. The ledger below\nstill records every comment, because a comment is often where dissent starts.\n\n## Channels\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/comments-standard.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Comments standard: dissent against a versioned claim beats free comments\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > $S/msg13.txt && git commit -q -F $S/msg13.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1","description":"Append research and the touchpoint map to trail #30; update the comments standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9157,"cache_read_input_tokens":260478,"output_tokens":1827,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":313},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1827,"cache_read_input_tokens":260478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RXwYYNpxWEhP3EddmRNiHd":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat >> $S/trail-commons.md <<'EOF'\n\nResearch on the extraction benchmark (LLM agent, 2026-11-04; leads, NOT pinned; no figure may enter a price until its source is pinned):\n- Market (vendors' \"ESG data\" term): Opimas is the only running series. $617M in 2019 (primary summary); over $1B in 2021; $1.9B in 2023 (Reuters citing Opimas); about $2.2B forecast for 2025 (Responsible Investor citing Opimas, Oct 2025; paywalled). The method is proprietary. MSCI's Sustainability and Climate segment had $384.8M in annual recurring revenue at 30 Sep 2026 (MSCI Q3 release).\n- Share from nonprofit sources: NOT PUBLISHED anywhere the agent could reach. MSCI and RepRisk name NGO, academic and government inputs without weights. CDP itself sells data (cdp.net/en/data-licenses) and, in June 2026, announced a split with Permira investing in a for-profit arm. That case bears directly on the commons argument.\n- Precedents: Wikimedia Enterprise $8.30M revenue in FY2024-25 (audited); CDP £60.46M income in FY2024-25, with £10.62M of charitable trading that includes data sales (not broken out); OpenCorporates offers free share-alike or paid plans (no revenue found).\n- Training-data prices: Reddit, $203.0M in aggregate data-licensing contracts over 2–3 years (S-1, primary); News Corp and OpenAI, over $250M over five years (WSJ, from sources).\n- To compute the nonprofit share properly: vendor revenue by product line (Opimas, paywalled); which inputs feed which product (methodology documents); input weights (possibly surfaced by the EU ESG ratings regulation's transparency rules); upstream licence fees actually paid; and an allocation rule between raw inputs and vendor analysis. Each is a research task in its own right.\n\nTouchpoint map (draft, Sloane's tray: touchpoints.html): every way people touch the commons (read, cite, dissent, bring evidence, answer questions, take a task, contribute code, bring an agent, license data, train a model, report a vulnerability), with what exists, the workflow, the review, the representations asked, and open questions OQ-D1..OQ-L3 attached to each touchpoint. Principle (Sloane): verification, not comments. The verification chain (colophon) makes dissent clean: dissent names a claim at a version.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc=$?; python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/comments-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## Channels\\n\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## Dissent beats comments\n\nA free-text comment can't be checked, so it adds noise as easily as signal\n(Sloane, 2026-11-04). The verification chain at the end of every rendering\n(its colophon) gives each claim a version, a source and a result. The\nstrongest response therefore names what it disputes: a claim, at a commit,\nwith a reason and, where possible, a pinned counter-source. It enters as a\nfork of the argument graph, beside ours, not as an overwrite. The ledger below\nstill records every comment, because a comment is often where dissent starts.\n\n## Channels\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/comments-standard.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Comments standard: dissent against a versioned claim beats free comments\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > $S/msg13.txt && git commit -q -F $S/msg13.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1","description":"Append research and the touchpoint map to trail #30; update the comments standard"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d97f2817-f0e1-46d8-9f32-f50669721e75","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgj8fboPxmMAdhvLTVnbe","requestRef":"9f79fad2-32e1-4c95-b0d9-50aa0cc818ab","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a036748-8bfc-4862-9592-7c672830afb5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:15:38.213Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"8a036748-8bfc-4862-9592-7c672830afb5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"69a10f07-8250-4487-8d94-0b0eaa4800b5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RXwYYNpxWEhP3EddmRNiHd","type":"tool_result","content":"rc=0\n8a62279 Comments standard: dissent against a versioned claim beats free comments","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"955468e3-09f0-47ed-b5b0-ccd0d787be4e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:15:44.095Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"rc=0\n8a62279 Comments standard: dissent against a versioned claim beats free comments","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/comments-standard.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":6,"newStart":20,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Emitted files themselves are never committed; the record of them is."," ","+## Dissent beats comments","+","+A free-text comment can't be checked, so it adds noise as easily as signal","+(Sloane, 2026-11-04). The verification chain at the end of every rendering","+(its colophon) gives each claim a version, a source and a result. The","+strongest response therefore names what it disputes: a claim, at a commit,","+with a reason and, where possible, a pinned counter-source. It enters as a","+fork of the argument graph, beside ours, not as an overwrite. The ledger below","+still records every comment, because a comment is often where dissent starts.","+"," ## Channels"," "," Any channel works as long as its comments land in the ledger:"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/comments-standard.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d97f2817-f0e1-46d8-9f32-f50669721e75","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","root":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","branch":"ec-ai-corpus","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":14},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"srvo/anthropic-pbc","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a036748-8bfc-4862-9592-7c672830afb5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"115117a5-79d4-4d9e-bd35-a7f2b15861a2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:15:44.132Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"abdbf879f1c8baf4d3d130a8ccbe0672e594508c87565d961c1f493173127f1f","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"9f79fad2-32e1-4c95-b0d9-50aa0cc818ab","keep":221,"tail":["0e907a08143f502125117536f1872ab6f518819cf5f885e76833d6414b24631a","d704c3f5026da35a845a6fb8b488d5f7b0f196bf18ebd9ae7337658812930e48"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",222,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"d4406d8e5d85c8e1ae85f95b62847eb17ff8f65bef91cb12a968eadefe62ec73"}
{"parentUuid":"955468e3-09f0-47ed-b5b0-ccd0d787be4e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8hG82X2RwVoLPgroD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've drafted a map of every way people touch the commons: `~/tray/touchpoints.html`.\n\n**What's on it:**\n- **The principle: verification, not comments.** The verification chain at the end of every rendering, the colophon as you call it, gives every claim a version, a source and a result. That's what makes dissent clean: someone can say \"this claim, at this commit, rests on this quote, and here's a pinned source that says otherwise\". That then becomes a fork beside our argument, not an overwrite. Information from elsewhere comes in the same way, with its source, rights and terms.\n- **Eleven touchpoints:** read, cite, dissent, bring evidence, answer questions, take a task, contribute code, bring an agent, license data, train a model, and report a vulnerability. For each, the map gives:\n  - whether it exists today, partly, or not at all;\n  - the workflow and how it's reviewed;\n  - what we ask the person to represent.\n- **Your pull-request question, as it stands today:**\n  - Only Descartes has a contributor guide, a short one on its public mirror. Accepted pull requests get folded into the main source by the maintainer. Contributors must have permission to contribute the material, and must not include credentials or private material.\n  - Praxis and this repo have no guide at all.\n  - The review would check four things: tests, a byte-identical rebuild, no forcing a check to pass, and staying small.\n  - I proposed one more representation: an agent-written pull request names its model and prompt digest, the same rule as for claims.\n- **The open questions sit on their touchpoints, ten in all.** Dissent and code have the most. For example: is a reason alone enough to dissent, or does it need a counter-source? Do contributors sign off or sign their commits?\n\nThe comments standard now says the same thing as the map: dissent against a versioned claim beats a free comment. Committed and pushed as `8a62279`. The map is also linked from trail #30.\n\n**The research on your pricing benchmark is back:**\n- **Market size:** spend on what vendors call ESG data was about $2.2B forecast for 2025. Opimas is the only firm that publishes a running series, and its method is proprietary.\n- **The nonprofit share has never been published.** The vendors name NGO, academic and government inputs but give no weights. So the share you'd charge on has to be computed, and that's a research project in itself. It would need each vendor's revenue by product line, which inputs feed which product, and what licence fees vendors actually pay upstream.\n- **CDP is the case in point.** It already sells its data. In June 2026 it announced a split, with Permira investing in a for-profit arm.\n- **Reference prices:**\n  - Reddit has $203.0M in AI data-licensing contracts over two to three years, from its SEC filing.\n  - Wikimedia Enterprise earned $8.3M in 2024–25, from audited accounts.\n  - News Corp's deal with OpenAI is over $250M over five years, as reported by the WSJ from sources.\n\nNone of these figures is pinned yet, so they're on the trail as leads. None goes into a price until it is.\n\nThe map is a draft in the tray. Its design belongs in Praxis, and Praxis has another session's uncommitted work in progress, so I haven't put it there. Should it go in Praxis once that work lands, or straight into the central plan?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":269635,"output_tokens":1090,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":269635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0be8f78c-a2d4-4f99-989f-45c9d40911b1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgj8hFw7ciBAEQHNXLghw","requestRef":"115117a5-79d4-4d9e-bd35-a7f2b15861a2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1acd23a2-4e43-4633-bf37-5628f973df6b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:15:54.344Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
